       <TITLE>Love’s Ultimate Sign</TITLE>
    </HEAD>
    <BODY TEXT="#000000" BGCOLOR="#FFFFFF">
        <font face="Arial,Geneva,Helvetica">
<p>&nbsp;
<p>
            <center>
                <font size="+2" color=red>
                    Love’s Ultimate Sign
                </font>
            </center>
            <blockquote>
                <p>
                >From town to town, His Holiness did roam<br>
                He had no palatial palace for his earthy home<br>
                Yet, from a young handmaid’s humble womb<br>
                To a borrowed and blocked closed, tight tomb<br>
                Emerged Jesus, the Hero of the greatest story ever told<br>
                The Son of the Divine King, not adorned in gold<br>
                But barefoot, beaten, and robed in His Precious Blood<br>
                >From open wounds now caked with tearful mud<br>
                Carrying a wooden cross weighted heavily on His Shoulders<br>
                Scorned and spat upon by common criminals and Roman soldiers<br>
                Three times stumbling<br>
                While people stood by mocking Him and mumbling<br>
                Three times falling<br>
                While obediently following His Father’s calling<br>
                So ordinarily human and extraordinarily Divine<br>
                His Death on the cross was Love’s ultimate Sign!<br>
                <p>
                <p>
                <p>
                <p>
